{
  "description": "Budgets for AI APIs (FR-31, SEC-45, T-07). `amounts`: decimal text → micros (millionths) or null. `usage`: the usage an answer (`body`, its exact text) reports in each format → `{input, output}` tokens or null (the gate answers `upstream_usage_invalid`). `charges`: usage and an optional `cost` → `{tokens, micros}`, micros = ⌈(input × inputPerMillion + output × outputPerMillion) in micros / 10^6⌉. `requests`: a request body (exact text) in each format with the route `maxOutputTokens` → its estimate `{input: UTF-8 bytes of the body, output: its output cap}`, or null = refused with `request_unbounded` (a stream, more than one answer (`n`, `best_of`, `candidateCount`), no cap or one above `maxOutputTokens`, a tool the provider runs and bills itself (only `tools` entries of type `function`, Anthropic tools without a type or of type `custom`, Gemini `functionDeclarations`), or for gemini a key with `_` in the body or its `generationConfig`). `sequences`: steps against one budget, starting with nothing spent. `{now, request, estimate}`: refused (seconds until the period ends) when the spending — open estimates included — has reached `tokens` or the cost `limit`, else null and the charge of `estimate` is added → `{refused, spent}`. `{now, answer, result}`: the answer to that earlier request; the charge of the estimate comes off (never below 0) and the charge of `result` goes on (`{input, output}` usage; `uncountable` = the estimate itself; `not_charged` = nothing); when the period of the request has ended, the charge of `result` is added to the period holding `now` → `{spent}`. `spent` is `{tokens, micros}` of the period holding `now` (0 once it ended); both are capped at 10^15 tokens and 10^17 micros.",
